  "truthBoundary": "A31 verifies a bounded local privilege and authorization evidence contract over generated or explicitly supplied local case data. It can bind role definitions, principals, selector permissions, role-admin relationships, proxy/admin authority, multisig/timelock delegation, separation-of-duties rules, escalation scenarios, revoke/recovery controls, hidden privileged surfaces and deterministic replay receipts. It does not prove current on-chain role holders, real proxy/admin slots, multisig custody, timelock execution, absence of hidden business-logic privileges, qualified manual authorization review, customer outcomes, independent assurance, LIVE operation or paid readiness. Generated benchmark evidence must never be promoted to on-chain, reviewer, customer, independent or commercial credit."
